# Shared rsync exclude list for deploying apps/stabler -> prod.
#
# Used by the deploy scripts:  rsync --exclude-from="$APP_DIR/.rsync-exclude"
# Mirrored in CLAUDE.md ("Deploy procedure"), which points here rather than
# repeating the list.
#
# THE list. The deploy scripts carry no inline --exclude flags any more.
#
# They used to, because the two scripts disagreed on anchoring and nobody had
# measured what consolidating would change. Measured 2026-07-26 by diffing the
# two shipped file lists (rsync -rn --out-format='%n'): deploy_stabler.sh was
# shipping 20 files deploy_full.sh withheld -- .github/, every top-level *.md
# (CLAUDE.md, DEPLOY-SECURITY.md, todo.md, the blueprints) and all three
# deploy_*.sh -- while deploy_full.sh alone shipped stabler/docs/. Every file in
# the divergence was documentation, CI config or deploy tooling; no app code.
# So the union below is the safe merge: it withholds strictly more junk than
# either script did, and nothing prod executes.
#
# Anchoring: no leading slash = match at ANY depth. Use a leading slash when the
# pattern would otherwise eat something nested that we DO ship -- /*.md is
# anchored precisely so stabler/integrations/uzpay/README.md survives.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT the same thing as prod hygiene: deploys run WITHOUT --delete, so anything
# that ever landed on prod stays there forever. Adding a pattern here stops the
# next deploy from shipping it; it does not remove the copy already on prod.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# VCS + build output
.git
node_modules
dist
__pycache__
*.pyc

# Local git worktrees. Measured 2026-07-25: 1910 files / ~93M -- more than the
# app's own 934. Excluded by none of the three scripts until now, and since
# deploys run without --delete, whatever landed on prod stays there.
.worktrees

# Tool caches
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache

# JS linter/formatter config. Same category as the Makefile below: dev tooling
# that never runs on prod. package.json is NOT here -- Frappe's esbuild reads it
# during `bench build --app stabler` on the server.
eslint.config.mjs
.prettierrc.json
.prettierignore
vitest.config.mjs

# Agent / dev tooling, never part of the running app.
# .claude was already excluded everywhere; .superpowers (46 files) and
# agent-os (58) are the same category and were shipping in all three scripts.
.claude
.superpowers
.zcode
agent-os
graphify-out
.smoke
scratch

# Beads task tracker (Dolt working copy + hooks). Caught 2026-08-07 in a deploy
# dry-run: it was about to ship .beads/dolt/.beads-credential-key and the git
# hooks to all seven tenants, on a server that runs neither bd nor dolt. Prod
# did not have the directory yet -- and without --delete, the first copy would
# have been permanent.
.beads

# Local staging area for files on their way out: stale git lock files, tests
# superseded by a rewrite, an eslint baseline. Caught 2026-07-31 in a deploy
# dry-run, which was about to ship a leftover HEAD.lock to all seven tenants.
_to_delete

# Test suite: CI runs it, prod does not
tests

# Translation harvester caches (CLAUDE.md: never ship .tx_*.json)
.tx_*.json

# Archives + OS cruft. ._* is macOS AppleDouble: rsync from a Mac ships one
# sidecar per file it touches. Measured 2026-08-06 against a git-blob-SHA
# manifest of the prod tree -- ._CLAUDE.md, ._README.md and friends had already
# accumulated there, none of them readable by anything on the server.
*.tgz
.DS_Store
._*

# Local-only scratch that reached prod the same way. `iskelet` is a design
# skeleton dump, /stabler/logs holds the app's own local log files (prod writes
# its own under sites/), and the .bak-* pairs are pre-edit copies left behind by
# the i18n and skeleton passes.
/iskelet
/stabler/logs
*.bak-i18n
*.bak-skeleton

# --- consolidated 2026-07-26 from the deploy scripts' inline flags ----------

# Documentation. `docs` unanchored on purpose: it catches both the 3.3M
# top-level docs/ and stabler/docs/ (a backup runbook, not app code).
docs
/*.md
/*.html
.obsidian

# Sibling projects that live inside the app dir but are not part of the app.
# stable-erp-website alone is 58M. It is also the directory CLAUDE.md warns a
# wrong-cwd rsync would delete -- excluding it here means a stray --delete run
# cannot even see it.
stable-erp-website
professional-excel-export
recon

# Deploy + dev tooling. These carry hardcoded local paths (/Users/zafar/...),
# so they are actively wrong on prod, not merely useless.
deploy_*.sh
Makefile

# CI config: the forge's, not the app's. .gitlab-ci.yml is the live pipeline
# (origin = gitlab.com); .github now holds only a pointer at it plus the shared
# test-module list. Neither runs on prod. .ruff-version is the lint pin both the
# Makefile and the pipeline read — dev tooling, same category as Makefile above.
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.ruff-version
